An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Most items have an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md
(a few record instead in a design doc or a differently-named plan,
named in the item), and the planning/implementation/review process (who
plans, who implements, who reviews, which gates run) is
docs/plans/README.md.
Gate labels (decision-gated, consumer-gated) rank priority rather than
block work (VD 2026-07-17); where a later VD stamp schedules an item
after 1.0-0, the item carries that stamp.
Standing rule (VD 2026-08-06): gate an item IF we cannot think of
anything valuable it might enable - that failure, not the absence of
a caller today, is the only licensed gating fact. "consumer-gated"
below reads accordingly, and the gate lifts the moment a valuable
enabled model or use comes to mind. An existing consumer is
sufficient evidence of value, never necessary.

Standing fact (VD): large datasets are common, and multiple chains
remain the default. The "single-chain n >= 1e5" spelling this entry
used to carry is an agent paraphrase VD disowns (docs/decisions.md
dec-B50, VD 2026-09-08). The large-n performance items are live, not
consumer-gated.

Standing discipline (from the 2026-08-07 census): verify an entry's
status claims against git and live code before scoping from it;
re-run a full census before release.

A "door" below means a recorded, undecided question, not a task.

items
  bcf-latent-mixing: research door, no plan doc of its own; for the
    post-merge mixing research. The probit and logistic BCF chains mix
    slowly at large prognostic amplitude, and two gates carry that as a
    standing cost. The latent SBC arms stay out of the sbc.yaml matrix:
    their ladders fail the admission clause at |a| >= 5 on both links,
    with or without the amplitude rescaling move (docs/plans/
    bcf-latent-evidence.md, Decision 1). bcf-latent-exact.R's K = 3
    probit arm keeps the slow-chain statistic, its seed spread up to 7x
    its 400-batch se while unbiased pooled over 300 seeds, and fails
    about 3 quick runs in 100 on a correct sampler; left as is by VD
    2026-09-25 ("Leave it for now, but keep in mind that we have mixing
    work to do down the road and will perhaps want to revisit").
    Revisit both when a mixing change lands. The removed rescaling move
    is one candidate to re-measure there (docs/decisions.md dec-B127;
    restoring it requires the cache rule in docs/design/
    multiplier-combiner.md). research-open.
  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: research door, no plan doc of its own. In the
    EXTREME tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the prior) the chain is
    frozen-structure mixing that no amount of burn fixes; a principled
    remedy would target tree-structure mixing at high SNR (tempered
    early sweeps, restart-style grow proposals). Low priority - the
    regime only arises with a stale build scale swapped against a new
    response inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse
    updateScale = FALSE). Record:
    docs/plans/archive/bcf-sigma-residual.md sec 4 item 2. The gaussian
    SBC arm at its recorded settings (72000-sweep burn, thin 30, R = 200)
    passes sigma at 0.0602 against a 0.0917 band and flags prog3 and
    prog4 (0.1061, 0.1209) without the amplitude rescaling move
    (2026-09-24); it does not reach the tail regime this door names.
    research-open, decision-gated.
  binary-kforest-k1-reachability: open K = 1 as a shipped multi-forest
    configuration - one varying-coefficient forest with no prognostic
    partner, which is VCBART's shape (D4 of
    docs/design/model-space-survey.md). R/spec.R refuses numForests < 2
    by design; the engine already takes K = 1, so opening it is a
    bridge change (applyAmplitudeSpec) plus R and tests, NOT engine
    work. Gated on ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE: a new shipped configuration
    owes its own, which is why
    docs/plans/archive/binary-kforest-prior-default.md refused rather
    than opened it.
  capi-unwind-protect: closed but for one arm. A host draw callback's R
    error is now caught at the callback itself, where R_UnwindProtect can
    still turn it into a C++ unwind, so the engine's run frames run their
    destructors before the jump resumes; the engine raises into R nowhere
    (the prior draws and the predict fan-out throw, and the bridge and the
    flat entries convert), and the chain rng buffer is released before its
    own raise. What is left is not the engine's: the rng library's
    unimplemented-kind refusals in external/randomBase.c and randomNorm.c
    are C and still raise through R from under a run. Both are default
    arms over kinds the library implements, so nothing reaches them
    today; closing them means an error channel out of the C rng API.
  correlated-outcomes: AR-1 / serially-correlated errors. Longitudinal,
    panel, ITS and DiD compose today via a latent AR-state + nugget in
    the outer sampler, driven through the setOffset conduit; EXACT
    pure-AR-1 errors
    are a deferred ENGINE door - banded residual precision plus
    cross-leaf GLS leaf updates break per-leaf independence. It opens
    on a consumer demanding exact AR-1 errors. Record:
    docs/design/correlated-outcomes.md (A). causal-motivated,
    decision-gated.
  doc-freshness-guard-tightening: door, VD decision. The symbol rule
    in tools/check-doc-freshness.R accepts a cite when each component
    occurs anywhere in the target file, and the guard reads docs/design
    and docs/plans but not man/ or vignettes/ for content drift, so
    prose can go stale while every cite passes. Tightening either half
    (symbol inside the cited construct; content coverage of man and
    vignettes) will surface pre-existing drift needing a content re-pin
    pass before it can go green. No plan doc until ruled.
  equivalence-harness-seeds-axis: post-RC, re-record
    benchmarks/R/bcf-equivalence.R and multinomial-equivalence.R
    against independent per-scenario seeds in place of one chain's
    autocorrelated draws - a |z| bar over 40 correlated draws tolerates
    a shift of ~0.9 posterior sd per cell, which is why the statistical
    tier is decoupled from the gate. Record:
    docs/plans/bcf-cross-host.md sec 2.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales and low-rank kernels; gp() takes a
    fixed positive numeric lengthscale today. Sampling one needs a
    theta prior, per-sample theta channels in the state and flatten
    formats, and costs multiples of the draw phase per sweep (kernel
    cache invalidation per theta draw). A decision memo comes first
    (docs/plans/gp-followups.md). Value holds: GP-leaf BART as a
    surrogate for sequential design of computer experiments (arXiv
    1203.1078), where a FIXED lengthscale asks the user to know the
    thing they are estimating, and low-rank kernels serve the standing
    n >= 1e5 fact. decision-gated on cost, not on value.
  gpu-bart: the backend-seam design waits on frontier items 4-5, the
    informed-kernel and preconditioned-CG prototypes
    (docs/design/parallel-bart-frontier.md sec 5). Memo and falsifiers:
    docs/design/gpu-bart.md.
  grow-from-root: frontier 3.1's exact informed-proposal use of the
    shared cut scan (docs/design/parallel-bart-frontier.md sec 3.1).
  interaction-constraints: formal heredity (an ensemble lattice prior)
    - a fourth formal beside interactions(max.order, groups, forbid)
    plus a prior change. Value gate lifted: it enables
    functional-ANOVA BART (arXiv 2509.03317), for which dbarts already
    ships the hard-constraint half. Post-release, no fixed position: it
    happens, when is open (VD 2026-09-08, dec-B95). Owed there and not
    yet written: man/interactions.Rd states the two-stage workaround
    meanwhile, which today only the design doc does. Soft path-dependent
    penalties: gate STANDS, no model surfaced. Records:
    docs/design/interaction-constraints.md,
    docs/plans/archive/interaction-constraints.md.
  level-shift-capi: two flat C API entries so a host can move a constant
    between the forest and its own intercepts - a read of the occupied
    leaves' count and value sum (original response units) and an apply
    that adds c/m to every occupied leaf of every tree and c to the
    cached totals. stan4bart needs it for the shared level of its group
    intercepts, which is confounded with the forest's level and mixes at
    lag-one 0.97 to 0.99 (stan4bart docs/plans/re-scale-mixing.md); the
    host's draw is conjugate Gaussian, Jacobian one. The engine already
    performs the move internally (Chain::drawLevelShift, the
    multinomial combiner's afterCombine); constant leaf only, refused
    under a stale partition or a constrained leaf, empty leaves skipped.
    About 360 lines with tests. Post-1.0 minor append: the header is
    built for it and stan4bart gates on major equality plus a minor
    floor, so it does not precede the freeze. Do it after stan4bart's
    ridge move lands, when the shared level is the remaining failure.
  manual-gate-runs: benchmarks/R/composition-matrix.R, an executable
    oracle against docs/design/feature-matrix.md, runs in no workflow -
    run it once at the release candidate. Growing sbc.yaml past its
    6-of-26 which subset waits until it has run once on main. Both stay
    manual by decision (docs/plans/pre-review-cleanup.md s5).
  memory-wall-frontier: the live perf frontier. The fused pass's
    unmeasured legs - weighted, fp32 residual, move-phase child
    gathers, vector/function leaves, BCF/multinomial, monotone,
    growForestFromRoot, K = 8 - are enumerated at
    docs/design/memory-wall-frontier.md sec 11; an arm A/B on both
    architectures is the confirmation to demand before any arc lands,
    since the arm64 no-signal case inverts the Zen2 win.
  monotone-leaf-quadrature: coneProbability's adaptive-Simpson
    quadrature (src/bartcore/model.hpp) dominates the monotone
    branch-score profile - 3227 of 3232 samples - and no alternative
    has been benched. Record:
    docs/plans/review-2026-08-24/memos/monotone-branch-fill-bench.md.
  multiforest-mutation-gaps: two doors
    (docs/plans/archive/multiforest-mutation-gaps.md).
    BCF whole-data setData (n free, z required): KEEP UNDESIGNED,
    gated on a considered failure to find an enabled model - every
    verified multi-forest class holds n fixed, and the BART
    adaptive-trial designs that exist cold-start per refresh; survey
    in docs/plans/archive/runsbcbcf-repair.md ("setData door survey").
    Per-forest row subsetting: the residue is PHYSICAL COMPACTION -
    per-forest zero weight ships, and a per-forest mask is permanently
    refused as a spelling of setForestWeights
    (docs/plans/latent-subset-mask.md). Value lifted by the AFT
    mixture-cure class (Sun and Song, whose authors reimplemented bcf's
    tree code standalone to get it - github roxiesun/TBAFTcure);
    settle whether the subset forest wants its own cut grid before
    designing, since compaction and zero weight are not the same draw
    law (docs/design/model-space-survey.md D2). Design-gated, NOT
    scheduled (VD: revisit on a second consumer or a release want).
  multinomial-doors: three entry-point doors, post-RC (VD 2026-09-01).
    A formula interface for dbarts(family = "multinomial") - a formula
    LHS carries no count matrix; bart2's cbind(c1, ..., cK) ~ x form
    is the pattern to adopt if wanted. A dbarts.h creation path -
    construction is R-bridge-only (docs/design/feature-matrix.md
    [f4]); opens on a flat-C consumer wanting multinomial. The family
    token in xbart - bart has carried it since the front-door arc,
    and xbart additionally needs a multinomial loss defined, every
    loss it evaluates being written against one location.
    Per-forest masking is NOT a door - permanently refused, a
    category's margin being a log-sum-exp over the other K - 1
    forests. consumer-gated.
  negbin-real-dispersion: real-valued dispersion needs a
    non-integer-shape Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler
    exists, so it opens on one of two unlocks: a published exact
    real-shape primitive (the CRT-Gamma machinery drops in as
    specified), or a project-level decision to admit approximate MCMC -
    dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated gamma-sum,
    bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200), which the record calls its own arc
    rather than a rider, and which equally gates weighted-binary's
    fractional weights. The engine seams are in place. A Poisson family
    is the companion door. Records:
    docs/plans/archive/negative-binomial.md,
    docs/design/negative-binomial.md sec 2 and sec 7. decision-gated,
    scheduled after 1.0-0 (VD 2026-08-28).
  python-bindings: a pybind11 facade wrapper is prototype-scale.
    Horizon, likely out-of-repo. The engine is not R-free below the
    bridge: model.hpp calls three Rmath density functions
    (Rf_dnorm4, Rf_pnorm5, Rf_dt), and the sampler and chain headers
    reach R's print and error entry points through the external IO
    unit, so a non-R host also has to supply those. Two further
    contracts it would have to take over: host-side ingestion
    validation (CSC structure, categorical bounds, sparse metadata
    assembly) lives in the R bridge, and mixed/CSC stores hold
    lifetime borrows anchored by R protection.
    decision-gated.
  rc-gate: VD's own read of docs/plans/bartcore-review-tour.md, then
    the RC declaration. Both VD-held. The pre-RC surface decisions and
    their sequencing are docs/plans/prerc-surface-freeze.md.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle
    (docs/plans/repo-modernization.md): recheck the CI action pins on
    each push and bump when GitHub deprecates a runtime; wire codecov
    only if a public badge is wanted. The optional roxygen2 and NEWS.md
    migrations do not start unasked.
  sbc-family-tiers: two open arms (docs/plans/sbc-family-tiers.md,
    docs/plans/archive/runsbcbcf-repair.md): the monotone follow-on,
    the first arm the constrained prior draw unblocks; and the full-R
    ladder re-runs, whose commands the plan records.
  sbc-ordered-factor-arm: benchmarks/R/sbc.R carries no ordered-factor
    PREDICTOR arm - its ordered factors are ordinal RESPONSES - so the
    midpoint cut grid's posterior shift is adjudicated only at the four-
    level, single-tree shape the exact gate enumerates
    (benchmarks/R/categorical-exact.R's ordered arm) and by the coherence
    of the equivalence corpus's variable-selection reallocation. An arm
    over an ordered-factor design at a level count above n.cuts, with an
    interior level absent from training, would calibrate the grid at the
    shape a user actually hits.
  second-review-followups: three doors the second whole-branch review
    recorded, none with a decision yet - a negbin rootogram panel,
    ordinal log_diff_exp tail precision, and a negbin burn-in
    dispersion channel (bart2 negbin runs one run(n.burn, n.samples),
    so plot draws no burn-in segment). Records:
    docs/plans/release-candidate-review.md's wave-3 landing note; the
    review's own DEFER bin is
    docs/plans/review-2026-08-24/consolidated-report.md.
  setresponse-positional-arg-warning: drop the once-per-session warning on
    a positionally-supplied second argument to $setResponse (it now sets
    updateScale, not updateState) once callers have had a full minor cycle
    to move to named arguments. Scheduled for 1.2-0 (VD 2026-09-01).
  sparse-extensions: open halves of docs/plans/sparse-extensions.md's
    Status list. Linear leaf on sparse: value gate lifted (a linear
    leaf over high-dimensional sparse designs). Streaming range kernel
    and per-column u8
    widths: gate STANDS - perf/memory only with no measured win;
    reopen with numbers. setData on a CSC/mixed store and
    per-observation CSC mutation are recorded typed-ingestion doors.
  survival-followups: doors out of the survival family pair (records
    in docs/design/survival.md sec 6 and
    docs/plans/archive/survival-models.md): competing risks (value
    lifted; it is the named consumer of the multinomial
    counts-mutation reopen door,
    docs/plans/archive/multinomial-counts-mutation.md, and the two move
    together), left truncation / delayed entry (value lifted; the
    cheapest door, a one-argument expander change), a long-format
    ingestion mode for time-varying covariates, and cloglog link
    (gate stands - awaits a cloglog binary family). Continuous-time
    models are AFT, which ships.
    low-ranked.
  tree-mixing-proposals: research door - how is the BART posterior
    sticky, and what proposal mechanisms beyond the shipped four-move
    set would help? The move census ran; the same-variable cut redraw
    "perturb" is in the kernel at default weight zero (ab49f83a) with
    its detailed-balance gate (30472110). Its benefit stage (slice 3)
    has run and killed the move at the pre-registered w = 1, d = 0.16
    (d73fb4e0): the kernel stays at default weight zero as an opt-in
    with nil measured benefit, closing slice 4's nonzero default share;
    it stays through 1.0-0 by maintainer ruling 2026-09-14
    (docs/decisions.md dec-A47), revisited by the mixing research. The
    nog-node rule Gibbs draw "rule_gibbs" is in the kernel
    at default weight zero too (7fb166ca) and its benefit stage has run
    (50032833): it is the first kernel change to move C1's summed
    minimum ESS, +22 over twenty matched pairs at two seed blocks
    against a +8 bar and at 2.21 cut-scan sweep-equivalents, so its kill
    does not fire; its coverage regression against the control was a
    reference-arm artifact, dissolved by the 2026-09-08 re-measurement;
    the rule draw's default weight stays zero until the mixing research
    sets one (dec-B96, below). The starting forest's law, an exact
    rejection draw from the restricted prior, is revisited here too
    (dec-A10, VD 2026-09-26).
    Owed there: the equal-cost arm on a quiet machine (slice 2's
    rule-gibbs-balance.R has landed). Rotation, a Stage R0
    generator-only regrow census, the re-specified reallocation census
    and heated companion chains stay unscheduled, alongside the two
    brainstorm rounds (sec 15, 16). Durable record
    docs/design/tree-mixing-proposals.md (ranking
    sec 4.1 as amended, specialization addendum sec 12).
  veto-arc-doors: a per-sweep vetoed-leaf diagnostics counter,
    R-readable - none exists in src/bartcore, so it is an additive new
    channel (docs/plans/release-candidate-review.md wave-5a landing
    note). And aligning sampleTreesFromPrior's all-zero bare-root
    branch with the mutate path, which draws structures at the prior
    from the same state: init and mutate disagree about one law
    deliberately, no baseline reaches the branch, and alignment is its
    own scoped decision (docs/design/empty-leaf-veto.md).
  weighted-binary: arbitrary real weights on the binary families need
    a real-shape Polya-Gamma sampler; IPW is a pseudo-likelihood trap,
    and the approximate-PG decision is shared with
    negbin-real-dispersion. Integer-weight logistic ships via
    replicated latents, and probit refuses weights outright - no
    tractable weighted latent form. docs/plans/weighted-binary.md.
    decision-gated, scheduled after 1.0-0 (VD 2026-08-28).

absolute residual prior scale (decided, VD 2026-09-14)
  post-release, R only: chisq gains an absolute spelling,
  chisq(df, scale = lambda), which names the prior literally instead of
  through the sigest its quantile calibrates against, and ignores
  sigest as fixed() does. Additive - a new argument beside quant, no
  spelling retired, so no tombstone. The residual prior's one home on
  the family object is the surface it is added to (docs/decisions.md
  dec-B123). scheduled after 1.0-0 (VD 2026-09-14).

front-door rename (decided, VD 2026-09-08; docs/decisions.md dec-B75;
  LANDED 2026-09-09; plan docs/plans/front-door.md)
  bart2's removal in 1.1-0 is gated (VD 2026-09-23): before removing
  it, check every CRAN reverse dependency for a bart2 call, and keep the
  alias one more release if any remains. WeightIt and MatchIt call it
  as of 2.0.0 and 4.8.0 (release block).
  Every other tombstone expires at 1.1-0 too (dec-B76; the registry in
  R/tombstones.R, which inst/tinytest/test-tombstones.R fails once the
  version reaches its expiry): in that release delete the file, the
  stubs, forwards and once-per-session warnings it lists, the
  .onAttach message, and their NAMESPACE entries.

factor encoding (decided, VD 2026-09-08; docs/decisions.md dec-B78;
  LANDED; plan docs/plans/front-door.md)
  subset splits stay the modern default; the manual states the
  difference from BayesTree and why. Post-release research item:
  weighting a factor column's split probability by its level count,
  which the indicator encoding gave implicitly.

